; selftest-wipe.eval - handed to the runner by `Eval.ps1 -SelfTest`; must PASS,
; and the self-test reads its `step` line, the TALLY after it and the refused
; `rest until`.
;
; A WIPE STOPS THE CLOCK (code-review C443). Four bleeds far past any member's
; health down the whole party at their first bite (a tenth of a second in), and
; the twenty-second step must stop there and say so - `stepped N ticks (Ns) -
; stopped: the party was wiped` - with the TALLY's seconds equal to what it
; stepped. It used to run all twenty, the app on the title screen, and give no
; reason.
;
; ...AND `rest until` OFF THE LEVEL IS REFUSED (C444), where it used to switch
; rest on and report "rested 0.00s - still resting (hit the cap)". After the
; heal the same line is the CONTROL: in play it rests. (expedition.eval's rung 4
; was the plan's probe for this, but since spawn-rise its skeletons spend the
; first 10-14 s of the fight getting up and the party survives that rung.)
logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 5
tally reset
effect bleed 0 500 30
effect bleed 1 500 30
effect bleed 2 500 30
effect bleed 3 500 30
step 20
tally
state
expect-refuse rest until 900
heal
rest until 900
state
